{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-witness-4he","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:witness-4he","kind":"definition","title":"Pauli witness for ${}^4\\mathrm{He}$ (exact in $q$)","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hecke-normal-form","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-shell-closure-normal-form"],"tags":["pauli-witness","helium-4","doubly-magic","exact-polynomial"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.PauliWitness.witness_4He","text":"witness-4he.md","leanSource":"witness-4he.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:witness-4he\"></a><p>The <strong>Pauli witness</strong> records the antisymmetric channel dominance of a nucleus's Hecke normal form. For <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^4\\mathrm{He}</code> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z=2</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N=2</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A=4</code>), it is the exact Gröbner normal form in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_4(q)</code> after quotient ideals <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I_8 + I_9</code>.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  F_{\\mathrm{Pauli}}^{(4)} \\approx 0.812</code></pre>\n<p>The polynomial <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{net}(t)</code> has <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">12</code> terms in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Z}[t, t^{-1}]</code>, matching the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-multinomial coefficient <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[2]_t^2 \\cdot [3]_t = 12</code>. Both <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z=2</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N=2</code> are magic, so <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^4\\mathrm{He}</code> is doubly magic.</p>\n<p>The high Pauli factor reflects the strong antisymmetric channel dominance of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code>-particle. In the Hecke normal form, the alternating trace <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{tr}_{\\mathrm{alt}}</code> captures the full multi-generator correlation that the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2 \\times 2</code> transfer matrix cannot resolve.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-mass-binding-algorithms/witness-4he.md","heading":"Definition","number":"26.3.3","page":"b/def-witness-4he","qa":{"counts":{"pass":81,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":1,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.PauliWitness.witness_4He","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-mass-binding-algorithms/witness-4he.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
